## Why This Is Asked

Beginner security tasks often miss logs containing PII. This question tests practical, actionable steps to prevent leakage without disrupting features.

## Key Concepts

- Tenant isolation in logs
- PII redaction and masking
- Centralized, encrypted log sinks
- Least-privilege log access and audit trails
- CI validation for log content

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example: redactPII function for logs
function redactPII(record){
  const masked = {...record};
  if (masked.email) masked.email = masked.email.replace(/[^@]+@/,'***@');
  if (masked.phone) masked.phone = masked.phone.replace(/\d(?=\d{4})/g,'*');
  return masked;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you integrate this into CI/CD and log shipping?
- How would you verify in production that no PII is emitted in logs?

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses depth in securing supply chains, runtime enforcement, and incident response at scale.

## Key Concepts
- Software supply chain security
- Image signing and attestation
- Runtime attestation and enforceable policy
- Immutable audit logs, tamper-evident design
- Secure update pipelines and incident response

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-sign-verify example (Node.js)
const crypto = require('crypto');
async function verify(manifestPath, sigPath, pubKeyPath){
  const m = await require('fs').promises.readFile(manifestPath);
  const s = await require('fs').promises.readFile(sigPath);
  const pub = await require('fs').promises.readFile(pubKeyPath);
  const v = crypto.createVerify('RSA-SHA256');
  v.update(m); v.end();
  return v.verify(pub, s);
}
```

